Subject: [PATCH 0024] Repaint the interface on a slow clock and add a close trigger

A frame is pulled during an interface repaint, so the interface decides how
often the video advances. That is invisible on the home screen, where something
is always animating, but a live session showed the real limit: with the stream
window covering the interface, nothing inside it changes any more, Qt has
nothing to redraw, and the video stalls whenever the interface stops painting.

The interface window is asked to repaint on a clock of its own while the stream
window exists. While the video still shares the interface's frame clock, that
keeps it flowing; afterwards it keeps the interface drawn and set up, which is
where the decoder receives its device.

The compositor's close button cannot be aimed at without a display surface the
stream window does not cover, so a development trigger does the same thing:
creating /tmp/opennow-close closes the stream window, which must end the stream
exactly like a click on the close button does.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

diff --git a/opennow-qt/qml/Main.qml b/opennow-qt/qml/Main.qml
index 0ebbd830..cb1f839f 100644
--- a/opennow-qt/qml/Main.qml
+++ b/opennow-qt/qml/Main.qml
@@ -246,6 +246,18 @@ ApplicationWindow {
         }
     }
 
+    // Each frame of the stream is pulled during an interface repaint, so the
+    // window has to keep repainting even when everything in it is static: with
+    // the stream window on top the interface underneath shows nothing but its
+    // backdrop, and Qt would otherwise stop rendering and freeze the video.
+    Timer {
+        objectName: "streamWindowRepaintTimer"
+        interval: 8
+        repeat: true
+        running: NativeVideoWindow.mapped
+        onTriggered: window.update()
+    }
+
     Shortcut {
         objectName: "shellFullscreenShortcut"
         sequence: "F11"
diff --git a/opennow-qt/src/app/ApplicationStartup.cpp b/opennow-qt/src/app/ApplicationStartup.cpp
index 6acead99..2a295bd6 100644
--- a/opennow-qt/src/app/ApplicationStartup.cpp
+++ b/opennow-qt/src/app/ApplicationStartup.cpp
@@ -257,6 +257,19 @@ static int runApplicationSession(int argc, char *argv[], QString &restartExecuta
               image.height());
         image.save(path);
     });
+    // Development aid: creating /tmp/opennow-close does what the compositor's
+    // close button does to the stream window.
+    auto *closeTimer = new QTimer(&application);
+    closeTimer->setInterval(400);
+    QObject::connect(closeTimer, &QTimer::timeout, &application, [] {
+        const QString trigger = QStringLiteral("/tmp/opennow-close");
+        if (!QFile::exists(trigger)) return;
+        QFile::remove(trigger);
+#if defined(Q_OS_LINUX)
+        WaylandVideoSurface::instance()->simulateCloseForDevelopment();
+#endif
+    });
+    closeTimer->start();
     grabTimer->start();
 #endif
     QObject::connect(&controller, &AppController::restartRequested, &application, [&] {
diff --git a/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.cpp b/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.cpp
index 7a9020e6..e42016a5 100644
--- a/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.cpp
+++ b/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.cpp
@@ -427,6 +427,13 @@ void WaylandVideoSurface::setWindowed(bool windowed)
     emit windowedChanged();
 }
 
+void WaylandVideoSurface::simulateCloseForDevelopment()
+{
+    if (!m_mapped) return;
+    emit closeRequested();
+    dismiss();
+}
+
 void WaylandVideoSurface::dismiss()
 {
     if (!m_surface) return;
diff --git a/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.h b/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.h
index e63783c5..abbd096a 100644
--- a/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.h
+++ b/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.h
@@ -58,6 +58,10 @@ public:
     Q_INVOKABLE void toggleWindowed();
     void setWindowed(bool windowed);
 
+    // Development aid: behaves like the compositor's close button, so the
+    // stop-the-stream path can be exercised without aiming at a decoration.
+    void simulateCloseForDevelopment();
+
     [[nodiscard]] bool isMapped() const { return m_mapped; }
     [[nodiscard]] bool isWindowed() const { return m_windowed; }
     [[nodiscard]] quint64 committed() const { return m_committed; }
